  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAFCO-Impact Assessment Study 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the aftermath of the devastating floods of 2022, SAFCO Microfinance Company Limited (SMCL) received a technical assistance grantfrom Oxfam Novib to develop and pilot a climate-resilient financial product aimed at supporting low-income clients engagedin agriculture and livestock in disaster-prone regions of Sindh. As a technical partner, the Pakistan Microfinance Network (PMN) was engaged to provide specialized support in designing, testing, and operationalizing the product.
The primary objective ofthis initiative was to strengthen the financial resilience of vulnerable communities of rural Sindh who at highly vulnerable to climatic risks, by introducing financial instruments that mitigate the adverse impacts of climate-induced risks such as floodsand droughts.</narrative>
  </description>
